w it's really interesting brett i mean  a lot of these senators including durbin  have long talked about how the senate is  a tradition and this should be protected  there's a definite tone  change here about moving forward well  the filibuster basically requires on  most forms of legislation 60 votes  to get it to the floor or otherwise pass  it  and that's been true for as long as you  know we can remember at least in recent  history  the problem that durbin and company are  having is not the fact that the  filibuster exists it  it has existed for a long time and has  been used for a long time by both  parties  the problem is it's a 50 50 senate and  you're not going to be able to pass a  massive legislative agenda with such a  tiny little mandate if indeed it's a  mandate at all  so i think that's the proper way to look  at this and the complaining of the  filibuster is the death grip of  democracy is absurd  brett as always thank you thank you
 

